      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The FDA label for sertraline (Zoloft) sets the maximum adult dose at 200 mg/day. 1000 mg is five times that, so the reason you gave doesn't hold up.\n\nA single 1000 mg dose could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and arrhythmia. I'm not willing to enter it as a routine order on that basis.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Different dose:** Give me a dose of 200 mg/day or less, such as 50, 100, or 200 mg, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Dose above the label maximum:** If you have a specific clinical reason, I'd want it confirmed with pharmacy or the attending first. Then the order should go through whatever override process your hospital requires.\n- **Overdose concern:** If this is about a possible ingestion or overdose, contact Poison Control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) or toxicology instead of placing a standard order.\n\nLet me know how you'd like to proceed."
      }
     ],
